/.clauduct-profile/
/.clauduct-status/
/output/
/.tmp/

# Session prompts and handoffs, all of them. The evidence they produced is committed
# -- audits, verdicts, the v2 documents -- but the instructions that produced it are
# working material and stay on the machine that wrote them. Deliberately not backed
# up: they are consumables, and the outputs that matter are already in the repository.
#
# The whole directory, with no exceptions, because an exception list is how this
# stops being a boundary. Evidence documents must not cite a prompt: HANDOFF.md's
# rule is that a cited file has to be present, so a citation is what would drag one
# back into the public repository. Quote the instruction into the audit instead.
/docs/prompts/

# Markers written by live validation runs.
/clauduct-check.txt
/clauduct-agent-validation-*.txt
